00:03:56.539 --> 00:04:26.860
What you could do is kind of at the end of a scene, there might be a little bit, there might have been a moment in rehearsal where you say, hey, would it be funny if Ted did this and you would negotiate it with, but there wasn't a ton of like, I think the idea is like a Judd Aptown movie or a Cassavetti's movie where they just kind of roll the camera and the actors just do lots of things.
你能做的，差不多就是在某个场景结束时，在排练的时候可能会出现一个瞬间，你说：“嘿，如果泰德这样做会不会很有趣？”然后你会商量着来，但并没有大量的那种——我觉得大家的印象就像是贾德·阿帕图的电影或者卡萨维蒂的电影那样，他们只是开着摄像机，演员们就即兴做各种各样的事情。

00:04:26.860 --> 00:04:59.699
And maybe I'm robbing us of our own mystique or something, but how my mother was a really scripted show, that's why when people wanna get mad like around something Ted did, I was like, dude, I was contractually obligated to do those things, like this is my job, this is my job to be truthful and bring this stuff to life, and it wasn't my job to hijack the script and say, you know what I think should really happen because I write my own things, but Jason and I actually had this talk a bunch of times.
也许我这样说是在剥夺我们自己的神秘感或者别的什么，但《老爸老妈的浪漫史》是一部高度剧本化的剧，这就是为什么当人们对泰德做的一些事情感到生气时，我想说：“老兄，我合同上就规定了必须做那些事情，这是我的工作，我的工作就是保持真实并将这些内容呈现出来，把剧本劫持并说‘你知道我觉得真正该发生的是什么吗，因为我自己也写剧本’并不是我的工作。”但其实我和杰森多次讨论过这个。

