Like I know he felt more like put me where you want me, you know, like put me in coach.
我知道他更像是那种“把我放在你们想要的位置上，教练，派我上场吧”的心态。

00:05:50.500 --> 00:06:23.096
I think he felt I was I was very curious about what you guys were up to like I said I always look forward to the script I always I was I was both a fan and I was I think I it's hard for me to watch things and not try to look under the hood and see a little bit like oh this is really smart how they're developing this character or this character's coming back and isn't that a funny callback like I'm interested in the mechanics but I also and I think I said this before I'm pretty clear about what I'm on set to do I was not there as a writer I was there to be the actor, and I had my actor had on.
我觉得他对你们在搞什么名堂非常好奇，就像我说的，我总是很期待剧本，我既是一个粉丝，同时我也觉得——让我看节目的时候不去试图一探究竟、看看幕后、不去想“哦，他们这样发展这个角色或者让这个角色回归真是太聪明了，这不是很搞笑的呼应吗”，这对我来说挺难的。我对剧本的机制很感兴趣，但同时，就像我之前说过的，我很清楚我到片场是来做什么的。我不是作为编剧去的，我是作为演员去的，我戴着演员的帽子。

00:06:23.096 --> 00:06:29.300
But I think another kind of subtle subterating and part of me was like learning and observing and, and, and, yeah.
但我觉得我内心的另一种潜流和一部分自我其实是在学习、观察，然后把它们吸收进来。

00:06:29.300 --> 00:06:30.367
Yeah, that's cool.
对，这很酷。

00:06:30.367 --> 00:06:33.392
And, and you knew you were writing your own things.
而且你知道你自己在写别的东西。

